# .gitignore template for a folder embedded as a qmd collection
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to <folder>/.gitignore
#   2. Replace ALL_CAPS placeholders with actual values
#   3. Add sensitive file exclusions specific to the tool (section below)
#   4. Run: git init <folder> (if not already a repo)
#   5. Run: qmd collection add <folder> --name NAME --mask "**/*.{EXT1,EXT2}"
#   6. Run: qmd context add qmd://NAME/ "Description of this collection"
#   7. Copy references/post-commit-hook.sh to <folder>/.git/hooks/post-commit
#      and set COLLECTION=NAME + PATTERN=\.(EXT1|EXT2)$
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PATTERN LOGIC (whitelist via negation)
#   *       → ignore everything by default
#   !*/     → re-allow directory traversal (git won't descend into ignored dirs)
#   !*.ext  → whitelist only these extensions
#   Rules are last-match-wins. Sensitive re-exclusions MUST come last.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Step 1: ignore everything ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*

# ── Step 2: allow directory traversal ───────────────────────────────────────
!*/

# ── Step 3: whitelist safe text extensions (adjust to your collection mask) ──
# Uncomment the lines that match your qmd --mask extensions:
# !*.md
# !*.json
# !*.jsonl
# !*.toml
# !*.yaml
# !*.yml
# !*.sh
# !*.txt
# !*.py
# !*.ts
# !*.js

# ── Step 4: sensitive — re-exclude even if extension matches ─────────────────
# Add tool-specific secrets here. Examples:
# auth.json
# oauth_creds.json
# .credentials.json
# .env
# SENSITIVE_FILE.json

# ── Step 5: large / binary / runtime dirs — re-exclude ───────────────────────
# Add dirs you never want tracked (logs, cache, binary data, sessions). Examples:
# cache/
# logs/
# sessions/
# history.jsonl
# *.sqlite
# *.sqlite-shm
# *.sqlite-wal

# ── Standard ignores ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
